Reolink: follow a camera that rebooted onto a new DHCP address.

async_step_dhcp trusted is_connected(), i.e. the device coordinator's last
poll, and aborted ("sticking to IP") when a camera showed up on a new IP
right after a reboot; and when it did probe the new IP, the camera's API was
not up yet at its DHCP request. Either way dhcp then deduplicates the
(mac, ip) sighting, so the entry kept the dead IP until HA restarted. Check
the old IP live instead, and retry the new IP for up to 3 minutes.
Applied by ../remote.py as a custom_components override (hosts.nix
patchedIntegrations) until upstream carries it (~/projects/home-assistant-core
branch reolink-dhcp-follow-ip).

